From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Oct 2026 14:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(store): stop shadowing the compiled Store with a loose QML copy

The Store was the only one of sixteen apps loading its QML from disk at
every launch. marathon-app-runner prefers an on-disk entryPoint over the
compiled module (tools/marathon-app-runner/main.cpp), so this one install
step made libstoreplugin.so dead weight on the image.

It was right when it was written: the bundled Store was a "Coming Soon"
placeholder and the override carried the Flathub-backed UI. apps/store has
since become that UI -- it holds the same flathub.org/api/v2 client -- and a
diff of the two files is three imports, all of them unused in either copy.
So the override now costs a parse per launch and buys nothing.

It also cost real work. The vendored copy is what nobody could see was
authoritative, and an untracked rewrite of it was lost on 2026-09-01; the
nine "Binding loop detected for property text" warnings a session logs come
from this file too, and they will now be fixed once, in apps/store, rather
than in whichever copy someone happens to open.

With the file gone the runner falls through to findAppQmldirPath, builds a
wrapper that imports MarathonApp.Store and instantiates StoreApp, and the
Store loads exactly as the other fifteen apps do.

Patch 0011, which vendored the file, is removed alongside this.
---
diff --git a/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst b/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst
--- a/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst
+++ b/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst
@@ -449,15 +449,6 @@
 unset __cmd __SENT
 EOF
 
-# --- App Store: real Flathub-backed browser ----------------------------------
-# Replace the bundled `Coming Soon` Store QML with one that pulls live data
-# from flathub.org/api/v2. marathon-app-runner checks the manifest entryPoint
-# file on disk first (tools/marathon-app-runner/main.cpp:644); when present,
-# it bypasses the compiled libstoreplugin.so resource bundle. We drop the
-# replacement at the path the manifest already names: StoreApp.qml.
-install -Dm644 /work/src/marathon-extras/StoreApp.qml \
-    "$BUILDROOT/usr/share/marathon-apps/store/StoreApp.qml"
-
 # Install handler + state-refresh helper. The handler is invoked via
 # Qt.openUrlExternally("marathon-store://<verb>/<arg>") from the Store QML;
 # xdg-open routes the URL scheme through .desktop MimeType. Verbs accepted:
-- 
2.51.0
